  48: ## T3 — Create and fence request budgets
  49: Reasoning: D1 makes replays quota-free, which needs separate budgets so retries cannot become unlimited traffic; 
distinct outcome from fencing.
  50: Task: The insertion quota is charged only for a winning insertion (once among concurrent same-key requests; 
never more stored messages than the quota at the boundary with distinct keys); every create request consumes a 
per-user request budget; fence/lookup calls consume their own per-user budget; any exhausted budget returns 429.
  51: Done when: The AC-009 route-level clauses hold on the local database.
  52: Verify by: Messaging DB integration tests for each AC-009 route clause (replay does not reduce quota; 
replays/validation failures/quota losers consume the request budget; fence budget independent; concurrent same-key 
charges once; concurrent distinct keys at the boundary) pass; RLS review gate recorded.
  53: Covers: FR-008, AC-009, AC-035
  54: Root: T3
  55: Depends on: T2
