  93: ## T8 — Durable single-tab outbox with ordered automatic delivery
  94: Reasoning: The core of G1: write-before-dispatch, persistence across reload/close, ordered automatic drain; 
failure classes come next.
  95: Task: Every eligible text/reply send is written to a per-user IndexedDB outbox (key, conversation, content, 
reply target, requested mention IDs, send time, window start, order, state, generation) before dispatch and before the 
composer clears; pending items render with a text label; items drain automatically per conversation in order when 
connectivity returns; confirmed items become the normal message; the outbox survives reload and tab close; 
attachments/voice are never queued (Phase 4 behavior kept); if the outbox write fails or storage is unavailable, 
nothing is dispatched and the text and reply stay with the D5 message.
