 102: ## T9 — Outbox outcome handling: unknown, definitive, rate limit, expiry
 103: Reasoning: Distinct outcome from the happy path: classifying every response per BR-005 and resolving unknown 
items through the fence without loss or duplicates.
 104: Task: Responses are classified per BR-005: transient (offline, 429, 401 with valid session) retried 
automatically in order; unknown (network error/timeout, 5xx after reach, lease end) fenced before any cancel, expiry, 
or redispatch; definitive failures show text with "Tentar de novo"/"Apagar" and block later items of that conversation 
only; 409 retry resends under a new key; items not stored 24 h after send become "expirada" without auto-send, while a 
fenced-stored item resolves as delivered; manual retry of an expired item keeps the key and opens a new 24 h window; 
cancel is offered only for items known not stored and not dispatched.
 105: Done when: AC-003, AC-007, AC-008, AC-009 (drawer clause), AC-010, AC-038, AC-042, AC-043, and AC-046 (drawer 
clauses) hold in the real UI with real routes.
