  11: - **Online application method (T23 only):** the Phase 4 method (Phase 4 TRACK T2/T25): re-check `npx supabase 
migration list --linked` and the target catalog immediately before; apply only each reviewed file's SQL 
transactionally and record only its version; read back by statement hash plus catalog objects; smoke-check. Never 
`supabase db push`, `migration up --linked`, or broad `migration repair`.
  12: - **Supabase/RLS review gate (AC-035):** every migration, RLS/Realtime policy, repository, and API route change 
passes the `supabase-rls-reviewer` audit (users.id vs supabase_uid, server client + `auth.getUser()`, service role 
never replacing membership checks) before the task is done.
  13: - **Adversarial review gate (AGENTS.md):** each task's diff gets the cross-model adversarial review (direct 
Codex CLI, `gpt-6.1-sol`, effort `max`, read-only, per `delegation-anthropic.md`) before it is recorded done; findings 
fixed or rejected with reasons in TRACK.
  14: - **Test policy (BR-015, AC-036):** integration tests against local Supabase/Realtime/real routes and Playwright 
E2E only (`playwright.messaging-local.config.ts`, local Supabase); no unit tests; a touched unit test is replaced and 
deleted, recorded in TRACK. A new E2E spec counts only after 3 consecutive passing runs in Chrome and in Edge. Network 
shaping only (SPEC §15); no mocked Supabase, repositories, or code under test.
  15: - **Regression (FR-032, AC-033):** every task that changes server or drawer behavior ends with the messaging DB 
integration suite and the messaging regression E2E suite passing locally, plus type-check and lint.
  16: - **Presence touch points:** any change near sign-out or Realtime lifecycle follows the `presence-safety` skill; 
the Presence logout sequence is unchanged.
