  19: 
  20: - Local Supabase answers at `127.0.0.1:54321` (HTTP 200). Messaging DB suite `__tests__/messaging-db/*` 
(`vitest.messaging-db.config.mts`) and local E2E (`playwright.messaging-local.config.ts`, project `messaging-drawer`, 
forces local Supabase env) exist from Phase 4.
  21: - Create route (`src/app/api/messages/create/route.ts`): `clientMessageId` optional; repository 
`createWithClientKey` dedupes on unique index `(sender_id, conversation_id, client_message_id)` (migration 
`20261005000414`); no attempt generation, no fence/lookup route, no expected-sender field. `enforceRateLimit(…, 
'message:create')` (30/min, `check_rate_limit` RPC, fails open) runs for every request after the participant check, so 
replays consume the insertion quota today (FR-008 gap). Replay comparison covers content, type, reply target, 
attachments — no mentions (no mention concept exists in `src`).
  22: - `Message` type and feed/Realtime mappings expose no `clientMessageId` (grep of `src/types` empty) → FR-034 
gap; optimistic matching is content/time based.
  23: - `mark_conversation_read(uuid, uuid)` is SECURITY DEFINER, executable only by `service_role` since 
`20261004170724`, with no internal membership check; `get_unread_counts` still has Supabase default `anon` EXECUTE → 
FR-029/FR-030 gaps confirmed.
