41:Task: The create route accepts an attempt generation and an expected sender for keyed creates; it commits only when 
the generation is current for (sender, conversation, key) at commit time and rejects a sender mismatch without 
storing. A new fence/lookup route, for the caller's own key only, atomically returns the stored message or makes every 
lower generation unable to commit, rejects older generations, never creates a message, and rejects anon and other 
users' keys. The original submitted composition is stored for replay comparison. Create and fence responses carry 
`clientMessageId`; outcome codes follow BR-005 (403 `NOT_PARTICIPANT` incl. missing conversation, 400, 413, 409, 
stale-generation). Unkeyed legacy creates and existing route/RPC signatures keep working.
59:Task: A mention store holds application user IDs mentioned by a message, written in the same transaction as the 
first creation, only for conversation members at that time other than the sender; requested mention IDs are part of 
the stored original composition (changed mentions on replay → 409; unchanged replay after a recipient left returns the 
stored message); only conversation members can read mention records; no client can insert/update/delete them; messages 
fetched by members carry their mention IDs.
61:Verify by: Messaging DB integration tests (non-member and self IDs store nothing, changed-mention replay 409 with 
no change, forced mention-storage failure stores neither message nor mention, anon/non-member read denied, direct 
client writes denied, unchanged replay after removal returns stored message) pass; RLS review gate recorded.
75:## T6 — Redacted messaging metrics route
77:Task: An authenticated, per-user rate-limited route accepts batches of at most 50 events and 16 KB, only closed 
event/reason enums, bounded numeric fields, and conversation type; drops anything else; adds a server-derived app 
version; writes structured log lines containing only BR-013 fields; rejects unauthenticated requests without logging a 
metric line.
79:Verify by: Integration test against the real route capturing log output: valid batch logged with enums/version 
only; unknown fields, free text, out-of-range numbers, forged version absent from logs; > 50 events or > 16 KB 
rejected; rate limit rejects; unauthenticated rejected with no metric line; RLS/route review gate recorded.
95:Task: Every eligible text/reply send is written to a per-user IndexedDB outbox (key, conversation, content, reply 
target, requested mention IDs, send time, window start, order, state, generation) before dispatch and before the 
composer clears; pending items render with a text label; items drain automatically per conversation in order when 
connectivity returns; confirmed items become the normal message; the outbox survives reload and tab close; 
attachments/voice are never queued (Phase 4 behavior kept); if the outbox write fails or storage is unavailable, 
nothing is dispatched and the text and reply stay with the D5 message.
104:Task: Responses are classified per BR-005: transient (offline, 429, 401 with valid session) retried automatically 
in order; unknown (network error/timeout, 5xx after reach, lease end) fenced before any cancel, expiry, or redispatch; 
definitive failures show text with "Tentar de novo"/"Apagar" and block later items of that conversation only; 409 
retry resends under a new key; items not stored 24 h after send become "expirada" without auto-send, while a 
fenced-stored item resolves as delivered; manual retry of an expired item keeps the key and opens a new 24 h window; 
cancel is offered only for items known not stored and not dispatched.
111:## T10 — Cross-tab outbox ownership and leases
113:Task: All tabs of the same user share the outbox and show each item once; per conversation only the oldest 
unresolved item is eligible and one tab holds an atomic drain claim (lease: request timeout 30 s, lease 45 s) that 
ends on tab close/crash or expiry, after which another tab fences and resumes; on connectivity return a pre-outage 
attempt is superseded immediately under a new generation; no two create requests of one conversation overlap across 
tabs; cancel is atomic against claims and propagates to every tab.
115:Verify by: New E2E specs (two tabs, held create, tab close, hung lease, simultaneous online, cancel/claim race, 
network-log overlap check) pass 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; regression suites pass.
122:Task: Before every dispatch and fence the authenticated application user must equal the item owner; an identity 
change or sign-out in any tab stops drains in all tabs; late create/fence/lookup responses after a switch, or 
older-generation/cancelled-item responses under the same identity, are discarded without changing any view, item, or 
claim; items are held (not failed or deleted) only when the client auth state reports the session ended, and drain 
after the same user signs in again; another user never sees, sends, or deletes them; a 401 with a valid client session 
stays transient.
123:Done when: AC-012, AC-044 (client clauses), and AC-047 (switch and same-identity clauses) hold in the real UI.
124:Verify by: New E2E specs (session cleared/refresh revoked then C signs in, paused drain then switch to C, held 
real create/fence responses released after switch, cancel, or supersede) pass 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; 
regression suites pass.
139:Reasoning: Polling, typing recovery, and metrics all consume one per-stream health model; the banner is its 
visible output.
157:Reasoning: Client side of G4 on the T5 topic, with its own stream health and removal detection.
158:Task: Typing travels on the T5 private topic with payload limited to user identity and typing flag; the indicator 
stays visible during continuous typing and disappears ≤ 5 s after stop, blur, send, conversation switch, or tab close; 
names follow FR-018 in direct, group, and room conversations; the user's own sessions never show their typing; the 
typing stream recovers after drops; the app detects its own removal from a conversation through a signal independent 
of conversation access and leaves the topic within 5 s.
159:Done when: AC-017, AC-018, AC-019 (E2E removal clause), AC-020, and the typing clause of AC-015 hold.
160:Verify by: New E2E specs (15 s continuous typing sampled each second, stop/close/switch, 1/2/3+ typists, own two 
tabs + second device, removal of E while subscribed, typing-stream-only drop) pass 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and 
Edge; regression suites pass.
184:Reasoning: Extends the Phase 4 notification claim with mention eligibility, emission-time authorization, and 
browser-wide suppression.
185:Task: With the Phase 4 toggle on and permission granted, a mentioned user gets one notification per message (DM, 
group, room, thread reply) titled "<Autor> mencionou você em <conversa>" with the full text, opening the conversation 
on click; emission is authorized with authoritative data under the current identity, then re-checked without further 
awaits for same signed-in user and no received removal signal; account switch or sign-out discards pending 
notifications; no tab notifies while any of the user's tabs in the browser is visible on that conversation; DM/group 
messages are never notified twice.
187:Verify by: New E2E specs (hidden tab, room with/without mention, DM and thread-reply mention, two-tab race with 
hidden tab first, own message, toggle off, two hidden tabs, held authorization with removal and account switch) pass 3 
consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; `messaging-desktop-notifications.spec.ts` passes.
192:## T19 — Client messaging metrics that never affect messaging
194:Task: The client records send latency, outbox wait, send outcomes by reason, stream drops/recoveries/outage 
duration, and polling activations/duration in a bounded buffer (oldest dropped), delivering fire-and-forget batches (≤ 
50 events, ≤ 16 KB, one in flight, aborted after 5 s, dropped under overload) to the T6 route; messaging never awaits 
metrics.
196:Verify by: E2E spec producing the three episodes with a log scan, plus failing, hanging, and flooded route runs 
asserting AC-001/AC-002 timing, ≤ 1 metrics request in flight, 5 s abort, bounded buffer, no visible error; 3 
consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge.

